# MRL User Proposal Draft

## Project Title
MOSFET Electrical Characterization and Semiconductor Device Testing

## Project Objective
The goal of this project is to develop practical experience with semiconductor device characterization by measuring and analyzing MOSFET electrical behavior.

Initial analysis is being performed using simulated transfer-characteristic data in Python. The project will then transition to experimental measurements using MRL semiconductor testing equipment.

## Measurements
The project will investigate:

- Drain current vs. gate-source voltage (ID-VGS)
- Drain current vs. drain-source voltage (ID-VDS)
- Threshold voltage (VTH)
- Transconductance (gm)
- ON/OFF current ratio
- Device-to-device measurement variation

## Equipment Needed
- Semiconductor parameter analyzer
- Probe station
- Suitable MOSFET or semiconductor test devices

## Data Analysis
Measurement data will be exported and analyzed using Python to extract device parameters and compare different extraction techniques.
